========================================================================
SYNTHESIS
========================================================================

1. Exact reset races match the full closed-LL audit in the bounded windows.
2. The no-swap approximation fails only at compactified wall/tie or
   swap-sensitive resets in these windows; those are proof objects, not
   counterexamples.
3. Initial segments are visible as wall-ledger extremals: open LL measure
   stays zero while exact reset races still hit compactified LL walls.
4. The next proof target is a reset ledger theorem: every primitive system
   has at least one reset whose exact wall trace reaches closed LL before
   the next reset or short-left loss.
